# ubsan.supp — UBSan runtime suppressions for the in-container nginx + zstd build.
#
# Filters out long-known nginx-core UB that isn't our module's bug. Without
# these, halt_on_error=1 + abort_on_error=1 (set by t/asan.sh so OUR findings
# become hard test failures) would kill the worker on the very first request
# via these nginx-internal patterns.
#
# Format: <check>:<symbol-or-file>. Wildcards allowed. See
# https://clang.llvm.org/docs/UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer.html#runtime-suppressions
#
# Each entry below is the nginx-core minimum we have to suppress so the
# request hot-path can complete. If you add a new suppression here, write the
# nginx commit / file:line in the comment so future readers can audit.

# nginx-core dispatches output_chain handlers through a void*-ctx function
# pointer that doesn't match the registered prototype. ngx_output_chain.c:70.
# Fires on every request that produces output. Not zstd module's bug.
function:ngx_output_chain

# Same pattern in chain-write helpers used by H2/H3 framers; nginx-core casts
# through void*. Triggers on h2-truncation.sh requests.
function:ngx_chain_writer
